## 6. Decision tree — from surveillance investment to detection uplift

::: {.callout-note collapse="true"}
## How we derive the status-quo detection probability (`d_status_quo` = 0.048)

The status-quo detection probability is **derived, not elicited**. The chain of evidence is:

| Anchor | Value | Source |
|--|--:|--|
| Annual NMC pesticide notifications | 1,013 | `n_nmc_annual` — NICD NMC Annual Report 2023 |
| NMC-hospitalised case-fatality rate | 12.5 % | `cfr_headline_mid` (range 10–15 %) — Free State 2018-19 + NMC observed |
| StatsSA MACOD pesticide-poisoning deaths/yr | 2,620 | `n_deaths_statssa_macod` — StatsSA Causes of Death, 2023: Table 4.12: Accidental poisoning by and exposure to noxious substance (X40-X49) |

**Identification.** If notified cases have CFR ≈ 12.5 %, then the *full* true burden satisfies $\text{true cases} \times \text{CFR} = \text{deaths}$, so the implied true burden is $2{,}620 / 0.125 \;=\; 20{,}960$ cases/year (`n_true_burden_from_statssa_mid`).

**Per-case detection probability**:

$$
P_\text{detect}^{SQ} \;=\; \frac{N_\text{NMC} \times \text{CFR}_\text{NMC}}{N_\text{deaths,StatsSA}} \;=\; \frac{1{,}013 \times 0.125}{2{,}620} \;=\; \mathbf{0.048}
$$

**CFR sensitivity bracket** (CSV: `d_status_quo_lo`, `d_status_quo_hi`):

- Lower bound (CFR = 0.10): $P_\text{detect}^{SQ} = 0.039$ (implied burden 26,200)
- Mid (CFR = 0.125): $P_\text{detect}^{SQ} = 0.048$ (implied burden 20,960)
- Upper (CFR = 0.15): $P_\text{detect}^{SQ} = 0.058$ (implied burden 17,467)

**Why this replaces the v1 value of 0.45.** The legacy v1 figure was an expert-elicited *hotspot-cluster* sensitivity (binomial argument: at cluster size ≥10 even with per-case sensitivity ~6 %, at least one case is captured with probability ~0.46). That quantity answers a different question. The brief now uses the **per-case** framing — directly auditable from NICD + StatsSA published figures — and the v1 0.45 is retained only for `analysis_report_v2.qmd` back-compat as `d_status_quo_v1_hotspot`.
:::

